Because JavaScript is single-threaded, we can safely update state synchronously without locks. The decision is made synchronously, then we return an immediately resolved/rejected Promise.

We'll use a Map to store per-key state. The config includes capacity (max tokens) and refillRate (tokens per second). We'll store refillRate in tokens per millisecond for calculation.

